hadiths[99]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23894","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us from Uthman ibn Jubayr from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Advise me briefly, so he said: When you stand in your prayer, pray the prayer of one bidding farewell, and do not speak words you will apologize for tomorrow, and gather despair of what is in people's hands."
"23895","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abdillah al-Ma'afiri narrated to us from Abu Abdurrahman al-Hubuli who said: We were at sea, and over us was Abdullah ibn Qays al-Fazari, and with us was Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, so he passed by the one in charge of the shares, and he had set up the captives, and a woman was weeping, so he said: What is with her, they said: They separated her from her child, he said: So he took the child's hand and placed it in her hand, so the one in charge of the shares went to Abdullah ibn Qays and told him, so he sent to Abu Ayyub and said: What made you do what you did, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever separates a mother from her child, Allah shall separate him from his loved ones on the Day of Resurrection."
"23896","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to me from Yahya ibn Jabir who said: I heard the son of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari's brother mentioning from Abu Ayyub who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Lands shall be opened upon you, and levies shall be imposed upon you, and a man among you shall dislike the levy and slip away from his people and offer himself to the tribes, saying: Who will suffice me such and such levy, indeed that hireling is to the last drop of his blood."
"23897","Ali ibn Bahr, he is Ibn Barri, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Khawlani narrated to us, Abu Salamah Sulayman narrated to us from Yahya ibn Jabir al-Ta'i, the son of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari's brother informed me that Abu Ayyub wrote to him telling him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned it."
"23898","Al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, Abu Ruhm al-Sam'i narrated to us that Abu Ayyub narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes worshipping Allah, associating nothing with Him, establishing prayer, giving zakah, fasting Ramadan and avoiding the major sins, Paradise is his, and they asked him: What are the major sins, he said: Associating with Allah, killing the Muslim soul, and flight on the day of battle."
"23899","Al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Damdam ibn Zur'ah from Shurayh ibn Ubayd that Abu Ruhm al-Sam'i would narrate that Abu Ayyub al-Ansari narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Every prayer wipes away the sin before it."
"23900","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Ibn Hubayrah narrated to us from Abu Abdurrahman al-Hubuli that Abu Ayyub al-Ansari said: A bowl with onions in it was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Eat, and refused to eat, and said: I am not like you."
"23901","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Abu Qabil narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Nashir of Banu Sari' who said: I heard Abu Ruhm, the storyteller of the people of Sham, saying: I heard Abu Ayyub al-Ansari saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them one day and said to them: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, gave me choice between seventy thousand entering Paradise without reckoning and the stored reward with Him for my ummah. One of his companions said to him: O Messenger of Allah, will your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, store that? Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, then came out while uttering takbir, and said: My Lord, Mighty and Majestic, added for me with every thousand seventy thousand, and the stored reward is with Him. Abu Ruhm said: O Abu Ayyub, what do you think is the stored reward of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? The people attacked him with their mouths and said: What have you to do with the stored reward of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Abu Ayyub said: Leave the man alone. I will tell you about the stored reward of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as I think, rather as one certain: the stored reward of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is that his Lord says: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His slave and Messenger, his tongue confirming his heart, admit him to Paradise."
"23902","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Baqiyyah informed us, from Bahir, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, that Abu Ruhm al-Sam'i narrated to them, from Abu Ayyub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever worships Allah not associating anything with Him, establishes prayer, gives zakat, fasts Ramadan, and avoids the major sins, for him is Paradise, or he enters Paradise. He was asked: What are the major sins? He said: Associating partners with Allah, killing a Muslim soul, and fleeing on the day of battle."
"23903","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Baqiyyah informed us, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abu Ayyub who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, the Ansar cast lots as to which of them would host the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Ayyub won them, so he hosted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When food was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), some was gifted to Abu Ayyub. He said: Abu Ayyub entered one day and there was a bowl in it onions. He said: What is this? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent it. He said: Abu Ayyub looked up to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what kept you from this bowl? He said: I saw onions in it. He said: Are onions not lawful for us? He said: Yes, eat them, but I am attended by what does not attend you. And Haywah said: I am attended by what does not attend you."
"23904","Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Measure your food, it will be blessed for you."
"23905","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Bahir, and he mentioned the like of it."
"23906","Haytham, meaning Ibn Kharijah, narrated to us, Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Measure your food, it will be blessed for you."
"23907","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a informed us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Amr ibn al-Aswad, from Abu Ayyub who said: And Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdallah informed us, Ibn Lahi'a informed us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, he narrated to him, from Amr ibn al-Aswad, from Abu Ayyub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand of Allah is with the judge when he judges, and the hand of Allah is with the distributor when he distributes."
"23908","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a informed us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Amr ibn al-Aswad, from Abu Ayyub who said: And Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdallah informed us, Ibn Lahi'a informed us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, he narrated to him, from Amr ibn al-Aswad, from Abu Ayyub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand of Allah is with the judge when he judges, and the hand of Allah is with the distributor when he distributes."
"23909","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr, from Abu Ishaq the freedman of Banu Hashim, he narrated to them that they mentioned one day what is used for nabidh, and they disputed about gourds. Abu Ayyub al-Ansari passed by them, so they sent a man to him and he said: O Abu Ayyub, may nabidh be made in gourds? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding every pitched vessel in which nabidh is made. So he rejected gourds to him, and Abu Ayyub repeated to him the like of his first saying."
"23910","Yahya narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abdallah, a man of Yahsub, narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever separates a child from his parent in sale, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will separate him from his loved ones on the Day of Resurrection."
"23911","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Ishaq ibn Abdallah, from Rafi' ibn Ishaq the freedman of Abu Talhah, that he heard Abu Ayyub al-Ansari saying, while he was in Egypt: By Allah, I do not know what to do with these karabis, meaning the privies, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you goes to relieve himself of stool or urine, let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it."
"23912","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Layth narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Qays, the storyteller of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to me, from Abu Sirmah, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that he said when death came to him: I had concealed from you something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Were it not that you sin, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, would create a people who sin and He forgives them."
"23913","Abu Ja'far al-Mada'ini narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam informed us, from Sa'id ibn Iyas, from Abu al-Ward, from Abu Muhammad al-Hadrami, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, he stayed with me and said to me: O Abu Ayyub, shall I not teach you? He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: There is no slave who says in the morning: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, except that Allah writes for him thereby ten good deeds, and erases from him ten evil deeds, and they are for him with Allah equal to ten freed necks, and he is in protection from Satan until evening. And none says it in the evening except likewise. He said: I said to Abu Muhammad: Did you hear it from Abu Ayyub? He said: By Allah, I heard it from Abu Ayyub narrating it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"23914","Abu Sa'id the freedman of Banu Hashim narrated to us, Thabit, meaning Abu Zayd, narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn al-Harith, from Aflah the freedman of Abu Ayyub, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed below and Abu Ayyub above. Abu Ayyub woke one night and said: We walk above the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So they moved and spent the night in a side. In the morning he mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lower is more convenient for me. Abu Ayyub said: I will not be above a roof under which you are. So Abu Ayyub moved below and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) above. He used to prepare food for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and send it to him; when it was returned to him, he asked about the place of the fingers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and followed the trace of the fingers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), eating from where his finger traces were. One day he prepared food containing garlic and sent it to him. He asked about the place of the trace of the fingers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was said: He did not eat. He went up to him and said: Is it forbidden? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I dislike it. He said: I dislike what you dislike, or what you disliked. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be visited."
"23915","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abdallah ibn Ya'ish, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says when he prays Fajr: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable, ten times, they are equal to four necks, and ten good deeds are written for him thereby, and ten evil deeds are erased from him thereby, and ten degrees are raised for him thereby, and they are a guard for him from Satan until evening. And when he says them after Maghrib, the like of that."
"23916","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Ishaq, the nephew of Anas, informed us, from Rafi' ibn Ishaq, from Abu Ayyub, that he said: We do not know what to do with the karabis of Egypt, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to face the two qiblahs or turn our backs to them. And Hammam said, meaning stool and urine."
"23917","Sa'id ibn Mansur, meaning al-Khurasani, narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Laythi narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Shihab saying: I bear witness upon Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi that he narrated to him, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no man who plants a plant except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, writes for him reward according to what comes out of the fruit of that planting."
"23918","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam Abu Imran, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Hasten Maghrib prayer before the rising of the star."
"23919","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Rashid al-Yafi'i, from Habib ibn Aws, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and food was brought near. I never saw food greater in blessing than it at the beginning of our eating, nor less in blessing at its end. We said: How is this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Because we mentioned the name of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, when we ate, then one who ate sat afterwards and did not mention the name, so Satan ate with him."
"23920","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Asim, from a man of the people of Makkah, that Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah was commander of the army in which Abu Ayyub raided. He entered upon him at death and Abu Ayyub said to him: When I die, convey my greeting to the people and inform them that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah, Allah places him in Paradise. And let them go with me and take me far into the land of Rum as far as they can. The people spoke when Abu Ayyub died, and the people put on armor and went with his funeral."
"23921","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Ma'mar ibn Rashid dictated to me, al-Zuhri informed us, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to relieve himself, let him not face the qiblah, but let him face east or west. He said: When we came to Sham, we found privies made toward the qiblah, so we turn aside and seek Allah's forgiveness."
"23922","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when food was brought to him, ate from it and sent its remainder to me. One day a bowl was sent from which he had eaten nothing, in it garlic. I asked him: Is it forbidden? He said: No, but I dislike it because of its smell. He said: I dislike what you disliked."
"23923","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Wasil al-Raqqashi narrated to us, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when food was brought to him, took from it what Allah willed him to take, then sent the rest to Abu Ayyub, with the trace of his hand in it. Food containing garlic was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tasted nothing of it and sent it to Abu Ayyub. His family said to him, and he said: Bring it near me, for I need it. When he did not see the trace of the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in it, he withheld his hand from it and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, this food you did not eat from, shall I eat from it? He said: In it is that garlic, and Jibril, peace be upon him, seeks permission to come to me. He said: Shall I eat from it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, eat."
"23924","Waki' narrated to us, from Wasil al-Raqqashi, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub, and from Ata, both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How excellent are those who use tooth-sticks and clean with water. It was said: What are those who clean? He said: In ablution and in eating."
"23925","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, mentioning therein the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three nights; they meet, and this turns away and this turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"23926","Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibrahim ibn Abdallah ibn Hunayn, from his father who said: al-Miswar and Ibn Abbas differed, and once he said they disputed, about a muhrim pouring water over his head. He said: They sent to Abu Ayyub: How did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washing his head? He said: Like this, forward and backward. Sufyan described it."
"23927","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Hakim ibn Bashir, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is charity to a hostile relative."
"23928","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Sa'ibah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Su'ad, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water is from water."
"23929","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Ubaydah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Sahm ibn Minjab, from Qaza'ah, from al-Qartha', from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regularly performed four rak'ahs at the sun's decline. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what are these rak'ahs which I see you regularly perform? He said: The gates of heaven are opened at the sun's decline and are not closed until Zuhr is prayed, so I love that good rises for me therein. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you recite in all of them? He said: He said: Yes. He said: I said: Is there a separating salutation in them? He said: No."
"23930","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan then follows it with six of Shawwal, that is the fasting of the year."
"23931","Isma'il narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdallah al-Yazani who said: Abu Ayyub came to us as a raider, and Uqbah ibn Amir was over Egypt that day, and he delayed Maghrib. Abu Ayyub stood to him and said: What is this prayer, O Uqbah? He said: We were busy. He said: By Allah, my concern is only that people think you saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing this. Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: My ummah will remain in good, or upon fitrah, so long as they do not delay Maghrib until the stars interlace."
"23932","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Marthad ibn Abdallah who said: Abu Ayyub came to us, and Uqbah ibn Amir was over Egypt that day, and he mentioned the like of it."
"23933","Isma'il narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to the privy, let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it, but let him face east and west. Abu Ayyub said: When we came to Sham, we found seats facing the qiblah, so we turned aside and sought Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forgiveness."
"23934","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Simak narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he ate food, sent its remainder to Abu Ayyub. He said: One day a bowl containing garlic was brought, and he sent it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, is it forbidden? He said: No, but I dislike its smell. He said: I dislike what you dislike."
"23935","Yahya narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: I heard Musa ibn Talhah, that Abu Ayyub informed him that a Bedouin met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on a journey, and took hold of the halter of his she-camel, or the rein of his she-camel, and said: O Messenger of Allah, or O Muhammad, inform me of what brings me near Paradise and distances me from the Fire. He said: You worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakat, and join kinship."
"23936","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah narrated to me, from his father, from al-Bara, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out after the sun had set and heard a sound, and said: Jews being punished in their graves."
"23937","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Wasil narrated to us, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to use the tooth-stick at night two or three times, and when he stood to pray at night, he prayed four rak'ahs without speaking nor commanding anything, saluting between every two rak'ahs. And thereby that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he performed ablution, rinsed his mouth and wiped his beard from beneath with water."
"23938","Waki' narrated to us, Quraysh ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Abu Wasil who said: I met Abu Ayyub al-Ansari and shook his hand, and he saw length in my nails and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you asks about news of heaven while he leaves his nails like the claws of birds, in which gather janabah, filth, and dirt. Waki' once did not say al-Ansari. Another said: Abu Ayyub al-Ataki. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: My father said: His tongue slipped, meaning Waki', and he said: I met Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, but he is Abu Ayyub al-Ataki."
"23939","Yazid narrated to us, Abu Malik, meaning al-Ashja'i, narrated to us, Musa ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Aslam, Ghifar, Muzaynah, Ashja', Juhaynah, and whoever was of Banu Ka'b are my allies besides people, and Allah and His Messenger are their protectors."
"23940","Waki' narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ayyub, or from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in Maghrib al-A'raf in the two rak'ahs."
"23941","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray witr with five; if you cannot, then with three; if you cannot, then with one; if you cannot, then gesture with gesturing."
"23942","Yazid narrated to us, Dawud informed us, from Amir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable, ten times, they are for him equal to freeing ten necks, or a neck."
"23943","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, from Amr ibn Maymun, from a woman, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Say, He is Allah, One, equals a third of the Qur'an."
"23944","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibrahim ibn Abdallah ibn Hunayn, from his father who said: al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Ibn Abbas differed about a muhrim washing his head. Ibn Abbas said: He washes, and al-Miswar said: He does not wash. So they sent me to Abu Ayyub, and I asked him. He poured water over his head, then brought his hands forward and back with them, then said: Thus I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"23945","Waki' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdallah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifah."
"23946","Bahz narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abdallah ibn Mawhab and his father Uthman ibn Abdallah narrated to us, that they heard Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of a deed that admits me to Paradise. The people said: What is with him, what is with him? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has a need, what is with him. He said: You worship Allah not associating anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakat, and join kinship. Leave it. He said: As if he was upon his mount."
"23947","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Ali ibn al-Salt, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that he used to pray four rak'ahs before Zuhr. It was said to him: You regularly perform this prayer. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it, and I asked him. He said: It is an hour in which the gates of heaven are opened, so I loved that a righteous deed rises for me therein."
"23948","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Abu Sakhr informed me, that Abdallah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdallah ibn Umar informed him, from Salim ibn Abdallah, Abu Ayyub al-Ansari informed me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the night he was taken by night, passed by Ibrahim. He said: Who is with you, O Jibril? He said: This is Muhammad. Ibrahim said to him: Command your ummah to increase the plantings of Paradise, for its soil is good and its land vast. He said: What are the plantings of Paradise? He said: There is no might nor power except by Allah."
"23949","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, and Adi ibn Thabit narrated to me, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdallah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the two prayers at Jam'."
"23950","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Za'idah ibn Qudamah, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from al-Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from a woman of the Ansar, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Does one of you like to recite a third of the Qur'an in a night? Whoever recites: Say, He is Allah, One, Allah the Eternal, in a night has recited that night a third of the Qur'an."
"23951","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, from al-Bara, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out when the sun had set. He said: He heard a sound and said: Jews being punished in their graves."
"23952","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Warqa narrating, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and six of Shawwal has fasted the year."
"23953","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Layla, from his brother Isa, from his father, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to Allah in every condition. And let the one who responds to him say: May Allah have mercy on you. And let him say: May Allah guide you and set right your mind. Hajjaj said: May Allah guide you and set right your minds."
"23954","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Kariz, from an elder of the people of Makkah of Quraysh, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: A man found a louse in his garment and took it to throw it in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do not do it; return it to your garment until you leave the mosque."
"23955","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Ishaq, meaning Ibn Abdallah ibn Abi Talhah, narrated to us, from Rafi' ibn Ishaq, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not face the qiblah with your private parts nor turn your backs to it."
"23956","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash who said: I heard Abu Zibyan, and Ya'la narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Zibyan who said: Abu Ayyub raided Rum and fell ill. When death came, he said: When I die, carry me; when you face the enemy, bury me under your feet. And I will narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); were it not for my present condition, I would not have narrated it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah enters Paradise."
"23957","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, brother of Yahya ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, Umar ibn Thabit, a man of Banu al-Harith, informed me, Abu Ayyub al-Ansari informed me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever fasts Ramadan then follows it with six of Shawwal, that is the fasting of the year."
"23958","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdallah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage Maghrib and the later Isha at Muzdalifah."
"23959","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Hanash ibn al-Harith ibn Laqit al-Nakha'i al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Riyah ibn al-Harith who said: A group came to Ali at al-Rahbah and said: Peace upon you, O our master. He said: How can I be your master when you are Arabs? They said: We heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Ghadir Khumm saying: Whomever I am his master, this is his master. Riyah said: When they left, I followed them and asked: Who are these? They said: A group of the Ansar, among them Abu Ayyub al-Ansari."
"23960","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Hanash narrated to us, from Riyah ibn al-Harith who said: I saw a people of the Ansar coming to Ali at al-Rahbah. He said: Who are the people? They said: Your clients, O Commander of the Faithful. And he mentioned its meaning."
"23961","Abdallah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from a man, from Abu Ayyub who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray four before Zuhr. It was said to him: You pray a prayer you regularly perform. He said: The gates of heaven are opened when the sun declines and are not closed until Zuhr is prayed, so I love that good ascends for me to heaven."
"23962","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Adi ibn Thabit al-Ansari, from Ubayd Allah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, that Abu Ayyub al-Ansari informed him that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage Maghrib and Isha together at Muzdalifah."
"23963","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abdallah narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Lahi'a informed us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, that Aslam Abu Imran al-Tujibi narrated to him that he heard Abu Ayyub al-Ansari saying: We lined up on the day of Badr, and a scattered group from us advanced before the rank. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at them and said: With me, with me. And thus my father said, he said: With me, with me. Ma'mar said: A group from us hastened. And he said: We lined up on the day of Badr."
"23964","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abu Ruhm al-Sam'i, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever says in the morning: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, He gives life and causes death, and He is over all things capable, ten times, Allah writes for him for every one he says ten good deeds, and Allah removes from him thereby ten evil deeds, and Allah raises him thereby ten degrees, and they are for him equal to ten necks, and they are for him an armed guard from the beginning of the day to its end. And he does not do that day a deed that overcomes them. If he says in the evening, the like of that."
"23965","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Aslam Abu Imran narrated to them that he heard Abu Ayyub saying: We lined up on the day of Badr, and a group from us hastened before the rank. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at them and said: With me, with me."
"23966","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abu Ruhm al-Sam'i, that Abu Ayyub narrated to him that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in our lower house, and I was in the upper room. Water was spilled in the upper room, so I and Umm Ayyub got up with a velvet cloth of ours following the water, fearing water would reach the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I went down to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while anxious, and said: O Messenger of Allah, it is not proper that we be above you; move to the upper room. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his baggage moved, and his baggage was little. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you used to send food to me, and I looked; when I saw the trace of your fingers, I placed my hand in it, until this food which you sent to me, I looked in it and did not see the trace of your fingers. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, in it are onions, so I disliked eating it because of the angel who comes to me. As for you, eat them."
"23967","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I said to my father: A man said: Whoever prays two rak'ahs after Maghrib in the mosque, it does not suffice him unless he prays them in his house, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These are of the prayers of houses. He said: Who said this? I said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman. He said: How good what he said, or he said: How good what he transmitted."
"23968","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi narrated to me, from Imran ibn Abi Yahya, from Abdallah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever bathes on Friday and touches perfume if he has it, and wears of his best clothes, then goes out until he comes to the mosque, and bows if it seems to him, and harms no one, then listens when his imam comes out until he prays, it is expiation for what is between it and the next Friday. And he said in another place: Abdallah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik al-Sulami narrated to him that Abu Ayyub, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever bathes on Friday, and he added therein: Then he goes out with tranquility until he comes to the mosque."
"23969","Bahz narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Adi ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Maghrib and Isha at Jam'."
"23970","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Mubarak narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Jabir, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdallah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to pray Maghrib and Isha with one iqamah."
"23971","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Ali ibn Mudrik who said: I saw Abu Ayyub remove his leather socks, and they looked at him. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over them, but ablution has been made beloved to me."
"23972","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Sa'ibah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Su'ad, and he was an approved man of the people of Madinah, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water is from water."
"23973","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, narrating it, he said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days; they meet, and this turns away and this turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"23974","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to relieve himself, let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it, but let him face east or west. Abu Ayyub said: When we came to Sham, we found privies made toward the qiblah, so we turn aside and seek Allah's forgiveness."
"23975","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Hajjaj narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, and Rawh, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, from Ibrahim ibn Abdallah ibn Hunayn, freedman of the family of Ayyash, and Rawh said: freedman of Abbas, that he informed him, from his father Abdallah ibn Hunayn who said: I was with Ibn Abbas and al-Miswar at al-Abwa', and we talked until we mentioned a muhrim washing his head. Al-Miswar said: No, and Ibn Abbas said: Yes. Ibn Abbas sent me to Abu Ayyub: Your nephew Abdallah ibn Abbas greets you with peace and asks you how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash his head as a muhrim. He said: I found him bathing between the two posts of a well, veiled by a garment. When I made myself known to him, he drew the garment to his chest until his face appeared to me, and I saw him, with a man standing pouring water over his head. He said: Abu Ayyub gestured with his hands over his head, all of his whole head, bringing them forward and back. Al-Miswar said to Ibn Abbas: I will never dispute with you. Al-Hajjaj and Rawh said: When I introduced myself to him and asked him, he drew the garment to his chest until his head and face appeared to me, with a man standing."
"23976","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, I heard Abu Ayyub informing, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not face the qiblah with stool nor urine, but face east or west. Abu Ayyub said: We came to Sham and found privies made toward the qiblah, so we turn aside and seek Allah's forgiveness."
"23977","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from a man, from Abu Ayyub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray Maghrib at the breaking of the fast of the fasting person, and hasten the rising of the stars."
"23978","Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Makhul, and Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Makhul who said: Abu Ayyub said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four are of the practices of the messengers: perfuming, marriage, tooth-stick, and modesty."
"23979","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Marthad ibn Abdallah who said: Abu Ayyub came to us, and Uqbah ibn Amir was over Egypt that day, and he delayed Maghrib. Abu Ayyub stood to him and said: What is this prayer, O Uqbah? He said: We were busy. He said: By Allah, my concern is only that people think you saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing this. Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: My ummah remains in good, or upon fitrah, so long as they do not delay Maghrib until the stars interlace."
"23980","Rawh narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun who said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable, ten times, he is as one who freed four necks of the children of Isma'il."
"23981","Rawh narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Abi al-Safar narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, with the like of that. He said: I said to al-Rabi': From whom did you hear it? He said: From Amr ibn Maymun. I said to Amr ibn Maymun: From whom did you hear it? He said: From Ibn Abi Layla. I said to Ibn Abi Layla: From whom did you hear it? He said: From Abu Ayyub al-Ansari narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"23982","Rawh narrated to us, Malik and Salih narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, that Ata ibn Yazid narrated to him, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three nights; they meet, and this turns away and this turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"23983","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Salih who said: Marwan came one day and found a man placing his face upon the grave. He said: Do you know what you do? He turned to him, and behold he was Abu Ayyub. He said: Yes, I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I did not come to the stone. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not weep over religion when its people undertake it, but weep over it when others than its people undertake it."
"23984","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, and Shurahbil ibn Sharik al-Ma'afiri narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli who said: I heard Abu Ayyub al-Ansari saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning going in the path of Allah, or an evening going, is better than what the sun rises and sets upon."
"23985","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Layla, from his brother, from his father, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to Allah in every condition. And let the one who responds to him say: May Allah have mercy on you. And let the one who replies to him say: May Allah guide you and set right your minds."
"23986","Hasan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from his brother, he said: I saw his brother, from his father, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: Let him say: May Allah guide you and set right your mind, or he said: May Allah guide you and set right your minds."
"23987","Abu Asim narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Bukayr, from his father, from Ubayd ibn Ti'la, from Abu Ayyub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade tying up an animal alive to shoot at. Abu Ayyub said: If I had a hen, I would not tie it up."
"23988","Surayj narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr, from Ubayd ibn Ti'la who said: We raided with Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn al-Walid, and four strong men of the enemy were brought, and he ordered them killed tied up with arrows. That reached Abu Ayyub, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding tied killing."
"23989","Attab narrated to us, Abdallah narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to us, that his father narrated to him that Ubayd ibn Ti'la narrated to him that he heard Abu Ayyub saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade tying up an animal alive to shoot at."
"23990","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub, that he was in an upper room of his, and a ghoul used to come and take. He complained of her to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: When you see her, say: In the name of Allah, answer the Messenger of Allah. He said: She came, and he said it to her, and seized her. She said to him: I will not return. So he released her. He came, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What did your captive do? He said: I seized her, and she said to me: I will not return, so I released her. He said: She will return. He seized her two or three times, each time saying: I will not return, and coming to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he says: What did your captive do? He says: I seized her, and she says: I will not return. He says: She will return. He seized her, and she said: Release me, and I will teach you something you say, and nothing will come near you: Ayat al-Kursi. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: She told truth, though she is a liar."
"23991","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, and he mentioned this hadith with its chain, meaning the hadith of the ghoul. Abu Ayyub said: Khalid ibn Zayd."
"23992","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Zibyan who said: Abu Ayyub raided with Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah. He said: He said: When I die, take me into enemy land and bury me under your feet where you meet the enemy. He said: Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah enters Paradise."
